        "category": "steering",
        "title": "Loss of Power Steering Assist (Pump Wear)",
        "description": "2008-2011 Enclaves (and platform-mates Acadia/Traverse/Outlook) can develop a power steering pump wear condition that causes an intermittent drop in hydraulic pressure and sudden reduced or lost steering assist. The vehicle reverts to manual steering requiring much greater effort, most noticeable at low speeds and during parking. GM issued a Special Coverage Adjustment covering the condition for 10 years/150,000 miles rather than a formal NHTSA recall.",
        "solution": "Replace the power steering pump (and inspect/replace fluid and lines). Covered under GM Special Coverage for 10yr/150k mi on affected vehicles; otherwise replace the pump out of pocket.",
        "severity": "high",
        "confidence": "high",
        "symptoms": [
          "Steering suddenly becomes hard to turn",
          "Intermittent loss of power assist",
          "Heavy steering at low speed / parking",
          "Whining noise from steering pump"
        ],
